{"id": "q0125", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3907012978, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "The equation\n\\[x^{10}+(13x-1)^{10}=0\\,\\]has 10 complex roots $r_1,$ $\\overline{r}_1,$ $r_2,$ $\\overline{r}_2,$ $r_3,$ $\\overline{r}_3,$ $r_4,$ $\\overline{r}_4,$ $r_5,$ $\\overline{r}_5,$ where the bar denotes complex conjugation. Find the value of\n\\[\\frac 1{r_1\\overline{r}_1}+\\frac 1{r_2\\overline{r}_2}+\\frac 1{r_3\\overline{r}_3}+\\frac 1{r_4\\overline{r}_4}+\\frac 1{r_5\\overline{r}_5}.\\]\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0125.wav", "input_sha256": "1f52f81768ca778d1c9c32eca86e9b0e0335d7d7143914cec4d9a3689828ce13", "input_samples": 499200, "input_s": 31.2, "n_real_chunks": 32, "score": 0.967, "act": 0.9965, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Assuming the equation is \\[ x^{10}+13x^5+10=0 \\] and the requested sum is \\[ \\sum{k=1}^5 \\frac{1}{rk\\overline{rk}}, \\] there is a problem: this polynomial has two real roots, so its 10 roots cannot be grouped into exactly five distinct conjugate pairs of the form \\[ r1,\\overline{r1},\\dots,r5,\\overline{r5}. \\] So as written, the problem is ambiguous/inconsistent. If the intended polynomial or expression is different, please resend it in standard notation, e.g. \\[ x^{10}+13x^5+10=0 \\] and \\[ \\frac1{r1\\overline{r1}}+\\cdots+\\frac1{r5\\overline{r5}}. \\]", "expert_answer": "Assuming the equation is\n\n\\[\nx^{10}+13x^5+10=0\n\\]\n\nand the requested sum is\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^5 \\frac{1}{r_k\\overline{r_k}},\n\\]\n\nthere is a problem: this polynomial has **two real roots**, so its 10 roots cannot be grouped into exactly five distinct conjugate pairs of the form\n\n\\[\nr_1,\\overline{r_1},\\dots,r_5,\\overline{r_5}.\n\\]\n\nSo as written, the problem is ambiguous/inconsistent.\n\nIf the intended polynomial or expression is different, please resend it in standard notation, e.g.\n\n\\[\nx^{10}+13x^5+10=0\n\\]\n\nand\n\n\\[\n\\frac1{r_1\\overline{r_1}}+\\cdots+\\frac1{r_5\\overline{r_5}}.\n\\]", "transcript": "The equation x ten plus thirteen i quotient ten equals zero has ten complex roots r one overline one r two, overline r two r three, overline r three r four, overline r four r five, overline r five, where the bar denotes complex conjugation. Find the value of frac one one overline r one plus frac one", "asr_s": 1.67, "expert_s": 46.9, "expert_input_samples": 464000, "expert_input_s": 29.0, "expert_input_sha256": "d3d094e413f521f9f6134dc2321474793f397f52edd63013eb44b09686b85c9a", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 47.03, "relay_synth_ms": 140793, "onset_chunk": 28, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 500, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 500, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0125_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "108af10d02bd3da5534a72670950cd1cafe288631d234b56c2c1465a49e940f2", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 245.28}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0125_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "9a17951b33cdd987b470fb85d18307099faaee387cf59801d80e38eb66f70c3c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0125_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "fbfdd5fc853b379e31825592199df564f1b412792c529c7b607dcee3613a4d97", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.081, 1.145, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.082, 2.145, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.077, 3.133, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.074, 4.135, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.085, 5.149, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.081, 6.146, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.078, 7.137, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.079, 8.144, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.084, 9.15, 1, 0, 0], [9,