{"id": "q0436", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1849289570, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "67ad139c11ad192120e00f1f4cc28f36ec4dc2a78471efa94476f5caf342cabc", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "Why does Daenerys Targaryen want to rule Westeros?", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0436.wav", "input_sha256": "2db19ef3dbff49d41b06f73e90ac5a73ec5a733528d38b22158ea5cadc37e484", "input_samples": 48600, "input_s": 3.038, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.2055, "act": 0.9988, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Daenerys Targaryen wants to rule Westeros because she believes the Iron Throne is her birthright as the last surviving child of King Aerys II Targaryen, whose dynasty was overthrown during Robert’s Rebellion. She sees herself as the rightful heir and wants to restore House Targaryen to power. Over time, her motivation also becomes ideological: she believes she can be a better ruler than the corrupt and oppressive leaders before her, “break the wheel,” and create a more just world.", "expert_answer": "Daenerys Targaryen wants to rule Westeros because she believes the **Iron Throne is her birthright** as the last surviving child of King Aerys II Targaryen, whose dynasty was overthrown during Robert’s Rebellion. She sees herself as the rightful heir and wants to restore House Targaryen to power.\n\nOver time, her motivation also becomes ideological: she believes she can be a better ruler than the corrupt and oppressive leaders before her, “break the wheel,” and create a more just world.", "transcript": "Why does Daenerys Targaryen want to rule Westeros?\n", "asr_s": 0.61, "expert_s": 3.99, "expert_input_samples": 48600, "expert_input_s": 3.038, "expert_input_sha256": "2db19ef3dbff49d41b06f73e90ac5a73ec5a73